        "credit": "Hasani.S.Sajjad",
        "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "description": "with beginning of a year ,people of Iran and some other middle eastern countries, celebrate Norooz which is an Iranian  ceremony in the first day of Farvardin coincide with march 20 according to their ancient customs.in this ceremony ,people put seven specific items, terminologically starting with letter \"s\" in their houses from the first day of Farvardin till Farvardin 13s.\nThe main Seven-S / Haft-Sin , are :\nSabzeh : Sprouting /Grass (the symbol of rebirth and growth)\nSamanu : Sumalak (the symbol of power and strength)\nSenjed : Oleaster (the symbol of love)\nSomaq : Sumac (the symbol of sunrise)\nSerkeh : Vinegar (the symbol of patience)\nSeeb : Apple (the symbol of beauty)\nSeer : Garlic (the symbol of health and medicine)\nOther Symbols that start with letter \"S\" somtimes are:\nSonbol : Hyacinth (the symbol of spring's arrival)\nSekkeh : Coin (the symbol of matter, material world, wealth and prosperity)\n\nSaat : Clock (the symbol of time)",
